# Copy to configure/RELEASE.local (not in git) and set EPICS_ROOT for this host; the rest follows
# from the standard EPICS layout below. EPICS_ROOT must be written here: EPICS's
# RELEASE parser takes only EPICS_HOST_ARCH from the environment.
EPICS_ROOT = /home/<user>/epics
EPICS_BASE = $(EPICS_ROOT)/epics-base
SUPPORT = $(EPICS_ROOT)/modules
AREA_DETECTOR = $(SUPPORT)/areaDetector

# ADEncstream's support modules are normally supplied by areaDetector's own
# $(AREA_DETECTOR)/configure/RELEASE_PRODS.local, which configure/RELEASE includes. If your site
# has no areaDetector top directory (so that file does not exist), uncomment these and set the
# paths to your layout. ASYN, ADSUPPORT, ADCORE and BUSY are needed to build the library and its
# tests (BUSY for the base Acquire/AcquireBusy records and testDriverRecords); AUTOSAVE, CALC and
# SSCAN are needed additionally to build the example IOC.
#ASYN = $(SUPPORT)/asyn
#ADSUPPORT = $(AREA_DETECTOR)/ADSupport
#ADCORE = $(AREA_DETECTOR)/ADCore
#BUSY = $(SUPPORT)/busy
#AUTOSAVE = $(SUPPORT)/autosave
#CALC = $(SUPPORT)/calc
#SSCAN = $(SUPPORT)/sscan

# A static IOC (EPICS_HOST_ARCH=windows-x64-static, or any fully static link) must also define
# SNCSEQ, even when areaDetector's RELEASE_PRODS.local supplies the rest: commonDriverMakefile links
# calc's sequencer references (seq/pv) only when SNCSEQ is set, and a static link has no calc.dll to
# bind them transitively. A shared/DLL build does not need it.
#SNCSEQ = $(SUPPORT)/sncseq
